The attached image is a Western blot (Figure 7D) illustrating the molecular forms of IL-1β in the supernatant and cell lysate of BMDCs stimulated with LPS, Nano-11, or both. It shows that LPS alone primarily induces the inactive 30 kD pro-IL-1β in cell lysates, with little secreted active IL-1β. In contrast, Nano-11, especially when combined with LPS, leads to a prominent band for the active 17 kD IL-1β in the supernatant, along with the 30 kD pro-IL-1β in the cell lysate. This confirms that Nano-11 induces the cleavage and secretion of the biologically active form of the pro-inflammatory cytokine IL-1β.